XBWorld Ruleset
===============

Custom ruleset for XBWorld, based on the webperimental ruleset (which
itself derives from the classic ruleset via fcweb).

This ruleset is designed for AI-agent games and can be freely modified
to experiment with game mechanics, balance, and new features.

Customization Guide
-------------------

- techs.ruleset     — Tech tree (add/remove techs, change prerequisites)
- units.ruleset     — Unit stats (attack, defense, HP, movement, cost)
- buildings.ruleset — Buildings and wonders (effects, cost, prerequisites)
- effects.ruleset   — Numeric effects of buildings/governments/techs
- governments.ruleset — Government types and their bonuses
- terrain.ruleset   — Terrain types (output, movement cost)
- game.ruleset      — Global params (start units, victory conditions, turn limit)
- cities.ruleset    — City parameters (citizens, specialists)
- nations.ruleset   — Civilizations/nations
- script.lua        — Lua event scripts (custom triggers, special events)

Inherited from webperimental
----------------------------

- Diplomat available from Alphabet
- AI players created with random trait values
- Spies can steal gold from enemy cities/capitals (needs Banking)
- Spies can steal parts of other player's world map
- Explorers can establish embassies once Writing is discovered
- Cities can be founded within enemy borders during war
- Zone of Control rules are turned off
- A player that knows Electricity has no fog of war inside their borders
- Leader unit in default startunits (losing Leader = losing the game)
- All units can be airlifted (light from Flight, medium from Advanced
  Flight, heavy from Fusion Power)
- Default map generator is Fair Islands (identical start positions)
- Howitzer and Battleship can bombard (3 tiles range)
- Alliance has deeper consequences (unit transfer, wonder help, shared
  bonuses from Sun Tzu, Bach, A. Smith)
- Default minimum distance between cities is 3
